  "fourth_down": {
   "id": "stone-fourth-down-rule",
   "source": "Stone's standing fourth-down rule (user, October 18, 2026, with his answers \"FG to 52 yards\", \"Go past midfield\" and \"Tice's first call\"): fourth-and-2 or less, go, with Tice's first call on the matching menu; fourth-and-3 or 4, go on the opponent's side of midfield, otherwise the field goal or the punt by the field-goal line; fourth-and-5 or more, a field goal when the kick is 52 yards or less, otherwise a punt. A kick is the line of scrimmage plus the bound fourth-down artifact's field-goal snap offset (library/data/2010_2014w4_fourth_down_decisions.json field_goal_offset, modal 18), so a 52-yard kick is the opponent's 34 and the field-goal line is the 34; past midfield is the opponent's 49 and in.",
